{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #155", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>In what ratio must a grocer mix two types of sugar costing Rs. 18/kg and Rs. 25/kg, so that the resultant mixture costs Rs. 21/kg?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2369;.18/kg &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;.25/kg &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2352;&#2369;.21/kg &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["1 : 3", "2 : 1", "4 : 3", "3 : 2"], "options_hi": ["1 : 3", "2 : 1", "4 : 3", "3 : 2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=290 height=232 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25022/image002.gif\"></p><p>Required ratio = 4 : 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=290 height=232 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25022/image002.gif\"></p><p>Required ratio = 4 : 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A mixture of 220 litres contains milk and water in the ratio 4: 7 respectively. What quantity of milk should be added to the mixture to reverse the ratio of milk and water?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>220 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4: 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2313;&#2354;&#2335;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["132 liters", "143 liters", "154 liters", "165 liters"], "options_hi": ["132 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "143 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "154 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "165 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Initial quantity of mixture = 220 liters</p><p>Initial quantity of milk = 220 * 4/(4 + 7) = 80 liters</p><p>And, initial quantity of water = 220  -  80 = 140 liters</p><p>Let x litres milk is added to the mixture. Then,</p><p>7: 4 = (80 + x): 140</p><p><b>x = 165 liters</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Initial quantity of mixture = 220 liters</p><p>Initial quantity of milk = 220 * 4/(4 + 7) = 80 liters</p><p>And, initial quantity of water = 220  -  80 = 140 liters</p><p>Let x litres milk is added to the mixture. Then,</p><p>7: 4 = (80 + x): 140</p><p><b>x = 165 liters</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A mixture P is formed by mixing milk and water from beakers A and B in the ratio 3: 4 respectively. Initially, beakers A contains 60 litres milk and beaker B contains 40 litres water. After mixing, the remaining quantity of milk in beaker A is 24 litres more than the remaining quantity of water in beaker B, then what is the quantity of mixture P?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; P &#2348;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3:4 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 60 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2348;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2341;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; P &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["35 liters", "21 liters", "42 liters", "28 liters"], "options_hi": ["35 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "21 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "42 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "28 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the quantity of milk and water in mixture P are '3a' litres and '4a' litres respectively.</p><p>Then, the remaining quantity of milk in beaker A = 60  -  3a</p><p>And, the remaining quantity of water in beaker B = 40  -  4a</p><p>Then, 60  -  3a = 40  -  4a + 24</p><p>a = 4</p><p>Therefore, quantity of mixture P = 3a + 4a = 7a = 7 * 4 = <b>28 litres</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the quantity of milk and water in mixture P are '3a' litres and '4a' litres respectively.</p><p>Then, the remaining quantity of milk in beaker A = 60  -  3a</p><p>And, the remaining quantity of water in beaker B = 40  -  4a</p><p>Then, 60  -  3a = 40  -  4a + 24</p><p>a = 4</p><p>Therefore, quantity of mixture P = 3a + 4a = 7a = 7 * 4 = <b>28 litres</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Two vessel A and B contain spirit and water in the ratio of 3:5 and 4:17 respectively. Vessel A has 27 liters of spirit. Find the total water content in both vessels A and B together if the total spirit in both vessels together is 43 liters.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3:5 &#2324;&#2352; 4:17 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 27 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; 43 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["68 liters", "113 liters", "45 liters", "23 liters"], "options_hi": ["68 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "113 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "45 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "23 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>In vessel A spirit = 27 liters</p><p>Ratio of spirit to water = 3:5</p><p>Water in vessel A = 5/3 *27= 45 liters</p><p>Total spirit in vessel A and B = 43 liters</p><p>Spirit in vessel B = 43  -  27 = 16 liters</p><p>Ratio of spirit to water = 4:17</p><p>Water in vessel B = 17/4*16 = 68 liters</p><p>Total water in both vessel A and B = 68+45= 113 liters</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In vessel A spirit = 27 liters</p><p>Ratio of spirit to water = 3:5</p><p>Water in vessel A = 5/3 *27= 45 liters</p><p>Total spirit in vessel A and B = 43 liters</p><p>Spirit in vessel B = 43  -  27 = 16 liters</p><p>Ratio of spirit to water = 4:17</p><p>Water in vessel B = 17/4*16 = 68 liters</p><p>Total water in both vessel A and B = 68+45= 113 liters</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of milk and water in a 91l mixture is 4: 3. Some quantity of milk is removed from the mixture, and the ratio of milk to water becomes 12: 13. How much milk is removed? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>911 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4: 3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 12: 13 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16l", "18l", "24l", "22l"], "options_hi": ["16l", "18l", "24l", "22l"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The milk in a mixture = 91*4/7 = 52l</p><p>The water in a mixture = 91  -  52 = 39 l</p><p>Let the milk removed from the mixture be 'x'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>(52  -  x)/ 39 = 12/13 </p><p>52* 13  -  13x = 39* 12</p><p>676  -  13x = 468</p><p>13x = 676  -  468</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16l</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The milk in a mixture = 91*4/7 = 52l</p><p>The water in a mixture = 91  -  52 = 39 l</p><p>Let the milk removed from the mixture be 'x'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>(52  -  x)/ 39 = 12/13 </p><p>52* 13  -  13x = 39* 12</p><p>676  -  13x = 468</p><p>13x = 676  -  468</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16l</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>How much quantity (in kg) of corn flour costing Rs. 63 per kg must be mixed with 40 kg of rice flour of costing Rs. 36 per kg, so that on selling the mixture at Rs. 58.5 per kg, there is a gain of 30%?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>63 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2325;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; 36 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; 40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 58.5 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 kg", "40 kg", "60 kg", "50 kg"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;", "40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;", "60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;", "50 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let k kg of corn flour is added. </p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(k * 63 + 40 * 36)/(k + 40) = 58.5 * 100/130</p><p>=&gt; (63k + 1440)/(k + 40) = 45</p><p>=&gt; 63k + 1440 = 45k + 1800</p><p>=&gt; 18k = 360</p><p>=&gt; k = 20 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let k kg of corn flour is added. </p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(k * 63 + 40 * 36)/(k + 40) = 58.5 * 100/130</p><p>=&gt; (63k + 1440)/(k + 40) = 45</p><p>=&gt; 63k + 1440 = 45k + 1800</p><p>=&gt; 18k = 360</p><p>=&gt; k = 20 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains 40 litres of acid. 5 litres of acid is taken out of the vessel and replaced by the same quantity of water. Next 5 litres of the mixture are withdrawn, and again the vessel is filled with the same quantity of water. Find the ratio of acid left in the vessel with the quantity of acid initially in the vessel</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2346;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; 5 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2354; &#2349;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["9:16", "49:64", "16:25", "25:51"], "options_hi": ["9:16", "49:64", "16:25", "25:51"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Remaining acid in the vessel = 40(1-5/40)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(1-1/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(7/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 30.625 litres</p><p>Hence required ratio is 30.625:40 = 49:64</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Remaining acid in the vessel = 40(1-5/40)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(1-1/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(7/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 30.625 litres</p><p>Hence required ratio is 30.625:40 = 49:64</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper has 500 kg sugar. He sold 220 kg sugar at 25% profit and remaining quantity of sugar at p% profit. If overall profit earned by him was 18%, then what is the value of 'p'?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 500 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 220 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; 25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; p% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 18% &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; 'p' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8.5%", "12.5%", "14.5%", "10.5%"], "options_hi": ["8.5%", "12.5%", "14.5%", "10.5%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total quantity of sugar = 500 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at 25% profit = 220 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at p% profit = 500  -  220 = 280 kg</p><p>Now, by Alligation method:</p><p><img width=379 height=255 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8531/image002.png\" ></p><p>Then, (18  -  p): 7 = 220: 280</p><p><b>p = 12.5%</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total quantity of sugar = 500 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at 25% profit = 220 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at p% profit = 500  -  220 = 280 kg</p><p>Now, by Alligation method:</p><p><img width=379 height=255 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8531/image002.png\" ></p><p>Then, (18  -  p): 7 = 220: 280</p><p><b>p = 12.5%</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the respective ratio of coffee powder of Rs.88 per kg be mixed with coffee powder of Rs.74 per kg so as to earn a profit of 20% on selling the mixture at Rs.96?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>88 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2313;&#2337;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 74 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2313;&#2337;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 96 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 20% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["2: 3", "5: 6", "3: 4", "4: 5"], "options_hi": ["2: 3", "5: 6", "3: 4", "4: 5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Profit% = 20%</p><p>Selling Price of mixture = 96</p><p>Then, Cost Price of mixture = 96 * 100/120 = 80</p><p>Now, by Alligation method:</p><p><img width=409 height=258 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8531/image001.png\" ></p><p>Therefore, ratio of mixture of coffee powder of Rs.88 per kg and Rs.74 per kg = 6: 8 = <b>3: 4</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Profit% = 20%</p><p>Selling Price of mixture = 96</p><p>Then, Cost Price of mixture = 96 * 100/120 = 80</p><p>Now, by Alligation method:</p><p><img width=409 height=258 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8531/image001.png\" ></p><p>Therefore, ratio of mixture of coffee powder of Rs.88 per kg and Rs.74 per kg = 6: 8 = <b>3: 4</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A can contains a mixture of two liquids P &amp; Q in the ratio 5:3. When 16 ml of mixture are drawn off and the can is filled with same quantity of liquid Q, the ratio of P &amp; Q becomes 23:17. How many millilitres of liquid P was contained by the can initially?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2376;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; 5:3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; 16 ml &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2376;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; Q &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 23:17 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2376;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; P &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["120 ml", "125 ml", "75 ml", "200 ml"], "options_hi": ["120 ml", "125 ml", "75 ml", "200 ml"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the can contains 5x and 3x of mixtures P and Q.</p><p>Quantities of P in mixture left = [5x-(5/8  X  16)] = 5x - 10</p><p>Quantities of Q in mixture left = [3x-(3/8  X  16)] = 3x  -  6</p><p>\\ (5x - 10) / [ ( 3x - 6) +16] = 23/17</p><p>(5x - 10) / ( 3x + 10) = 23/17</p><p>85x  -  170 = 69x + 230</p><p>16x = 400</p><p>x = 25</p><p>So, the can contains 25  X  5 = 125 ml of P</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the can contains 5x and 3x of mixtures P and Q.</p><p>Quantities of P in mixture left = [5x-(5/8  X  16)] = 5x - 10</p><p>Quantities of Q in mixture left = [3x-(3/8  X  16)] = 3x  -  6</p><p>\\ (5x - 10) / [ ( 3x - 6) +16] = 23/17</p><p>(5x - 10) / ( 3x + 10) = 23/17</p><p>85x  -  170 = 69x + 230</p><p>16x = 400</p><p>x = 25</p><p>So, the can contains 25  X  5 = 125 ml of P</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains 20L of liquid A and 27L of liquid B. When 'a' litre of both quantities is added to the mixture, the ratio becomes 4:5 respectively. Find the value of 'a' in litres.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; 20L &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; 27L &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; 'a' &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:5 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 'a' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; (&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["6", "8", "15", "1"], "options_hi": ["6", "8", "15", "1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=72 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20832/image024.png\"></p><p>100 + 5a = 108 + 4a</p><p>a = 8 litres</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=72 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20832/image024.png\"></p><p>100 + 5a = 108 + 4a</p><p>a = 8 litres</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A vendor bought two varieties of tea, brand A and brand B, costing Rs 80 per kg and Rs 140 per kg, respectively, and mixed them in a certain ratio. If he sold the mixture at Rs 120 per kg making a profit of 20%, then find the ratio of brand A to brand B tea in the mixture. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2351;, &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337; B, &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 80 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; 140 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 20% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 120 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337; B &#2330;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3: 4", "2: 3", "2: 1", "1: 3"], "options_hi": ["3: 4", "2: 3", "2: 1", "1: 3"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the selling price be Rs 'a'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>a * 120/ 100 = 120 </p><p>a = Rs 100 </p><p><img width=306 height=117 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23180/image003.png\" ></p><p>The required ratio = 2: 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the selling price be Rs 'a'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>a * 120/ 100 = 120 </p><p>a = Rs 100 </p><p><img width=306 height=117 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23180/image003.png\" ></p><p>The required ratio = 2: 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A container contains 96 ml of mixture of chemical A and chemical B in the ratio of 5: 7 respectively. If 36 ml of mixture is taken out from that container and then 40 ml of chemical B added to it, what will be the percentage of chemical A in the final mixture?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344; B &#2325;&#2366; 96 ml &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5:7 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 36 ml &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40 ml &#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344; B &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["12%", "25%", "50%", "40%"], "options_hi": ["12%", "25%", "50%", "40%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>A container contains 96 ml of mixture of chemical A and chemical B in the ratio of 5: 7 respectively.</p><p>Total quantity of chemical A = 96 * (5/12)= 40 ml</p><p>Total quantity of chemical B = 96 * (7/12) = 56 ml</p><p>Chemical A in 36 ml of mixture= 36 * (5/12)=15 ml</p><p>New mixture= 96- 36 + 40=100 ml</p><p>Chemical A in new mix= 40  -  15 =25 ml</p><p>Percentage of chemical A in final mixture= (25/100)*100=25%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A container contains 96 ml of mixture of chemical A and chemical B in the ratio of 5: 7 respectively.</p><p>Total quantity of chemical A = 96 * (5/12)= 40 ml</p><p>Total quantity of chemical B = 96 * (7/12) = 56 ml</p><p>Chemical A in 36 ml of mixture= 36 * (5/12)=15 ml</p><p>New mixture= 96- 36 + 40=100 ml</p><p>Chemical A in new mix= 40  -  15 =25 ml</p><p>Percentage of chemical A in final mixture= (25/100)*100=25%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Two liquids X and Y have the following compositions:</p><p>Liquid X has milk and water in a ratio of 2: 7.</p><p>Liquid Y has milk and water in a ratio of 11: 7.</p><p>If equal quantities of liquids X and Y are used for producing liquid Z, then find the ratio of milk and water in liquid Z.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p>&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2: 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Y &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 11: 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Z &#2340;&#2376;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Z &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5: 7", "7: 5", "3: 5", "5: 3"], "options_hi": ["5: 7", "7: 5", "3: 5", "5: 3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Part of milk in liquid X = 2/9</p><p>Part of milk in liquid Y = 11/18</p><p>Part of water in liquid X = 7/9</p><p>Part of water in liquid Y = 7/18</p><p><img width=159 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image026.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=35 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=27 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image029.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Part of milk in liquid X = 2/9</p><p>Part of milk in liquid Y = 11/18</p><p>Part of water in liquid X = 7/9</p><p>Part of water in liquid Y = 7/18</p><p><img width=159 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image026.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=35 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=27 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image029.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains a mixture of salt and water in the ratio of 2: 3. If 12 litre of water is vaporized from the mixture, then the quantity of salt and water becomes equal. Find the initial quantity of the mixture.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2 : 3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2350;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; 12 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2359;&#2381;&#2346;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2350;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["24 litre", "36 litre", "48 litre", "60 litre"], "options_hi": ["24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "36 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "48 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "60 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=529 height=68 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23256/image003.png\" ></p><p>The initial quantity of the mixture = 12 * 5 = 60 litre</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=529 height=68 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23256/image003.png\" ></p><p>The initial quantity of the mixture = 12 * 5 = 60 litre</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Solution A contains x% alcohol and Solution B contains (x + 10)% alcohol. When they are mixed in the ratio 2:3, the mixture contains 42% alcohol. What is the value of x?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; x% &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2377;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; (x + 10)% &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2377;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2332;&#2348; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; 2:3 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 42% &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2377;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["32", "36", "34", "38"], "options_hi": ["32", "36", "34", "38"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>(2x + 3(x + 10))/5 = 42</p><p>5x + 30 = 210</p><p>5x = 180</p><p>x = 36</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>(2x + 3(x + 10))/5 = 42</p><p>5x + 30 = 210</p><p>5x = 180</p><p>x = 36</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>280 L of mixture X is mixed with 400 L of mixture Y. If mixture X has milk and water in the ratio of 3: 4 and mixture Y has water and palm oil in the ratio of 9: 1, the amount of water in the new mixture is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2325;&#2375; 280 L &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Y &#2325;&#2375; 400 L &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3: 4 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Y &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2375;&#2354; (&#2346;&#2366;&#2350; &#2321;&#2351;&#2354;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 1 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["500 L", "520 L", "540 L", "480 L"], "options_hi": ["500 L", "520 L", "540 L", "480 L"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Amount of water in mixture X = 280 * 4/7 = 160 L</p><p>Amount of water in mixture Y = 400 * 9/10 = 360 L</p><p>Amount of water in new mixture = 160 + 360 = 520 L</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount of water in mixture X = 280 * 4/7 = 160 L</p><p>Amount of water in mixture Y = 400 * 9/10 = 360 L</p><p>Amount of water in new mixture = 160 + 360 = 520 L</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Liquid P and Q in two containers A and B, are in the ratio 9: 11 and 13: 5 respectively. In what ratio, the liquids in both the containers should be mixed to obtain a new mixture in container Z containing 50% of liquid P?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 9: 11 &#2324;&#2352; 13: 5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; Z &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 50% &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; P &#2351;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; &#2346;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["40: 9", "9: 20", "9: 40", "20: 9"], "options_hi": ["40: 9", "9: 20", "9: 40", "20: 9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Quantity of liquid P in container A = 9/20</p><p>Quantity of liquid P in container B = 13/18</p><p>Quantity of liquid P in container Z = 1/2</p><p><img width=222 height=140 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23664/image001.png\" ></p><p>Using Alligation Method,</p><p>Required ratio = 2/9: 1/20 = 40: 9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Quantity of liquid P in container A = 9/20</p><p>Quantity of liquid P in container B = 13/18</p><p>Quantity of liquid P in container Z = 1/2</p><p><img width=222 height=140 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23664/image001.png\" ></p><p>Using Alligation Method,</p><p>Required ratio = 2/9: 1/20 = 40: 9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>70ml of 60% concentration of acid X solution is added to 50 ml of 64% concentration of acid X solution. What is the concentration of acid X in the new solution?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>60% &#2360;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; 70 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 64% &#2360;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; 50 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2351;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; X &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["61.99%", "61.66%", "61.33%", "61.22%"], "options_hi": ["61.99%", "61.66%", "61.33%", "61.22%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Concentration of acid X in 70 ml of solution = 70 * 60/100 = 42 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in 50 ml of solution = 50 * 64/100 = 32 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in new solution = 42 + 32 = 74 ml</p><p>Required percentage = (74/120) * 100 = 185/3 = 61. 66%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Concentration of acid X in 70 ml of solution = 70 * 60/100 = 42 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in 50 ml of solution = 50 * 64/100 = 32 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in new solution = 42 + 32 = 74 ml</p><p>Required percentage = (74/120) * 100 = 185/3 = 61. 66%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In what ratio must a shopkeeper mix two varieties of tea costing Rs.231 and Rs.253 per kg, respectively, to get a mixture of tea worth Rs.243 per kg?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 243 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 231 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 253 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["6: 1", "2: 1", "5: 6", "3: 4"], "options_hi": ["6: 1", "2: 1", "5: 6", "3: 4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Using the Alligation method,</p><p>Required ratio = (253  -  243): (243  -  231)</p><p>= 10: 12</p><p>= 5: 6</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Using the Alligation method,</p><p>Required ratio = (253  -  243): (243  -  231)</p><p>= 10: 12</p><p>= 5: 6</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}